From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:32:44 +0000
Subject: Remove the Android XR feature module

The APK included Chromium's Android XR feature module. It brings the
ARCore SDK client, the Jetpack XR and Impress libraries, and about
20 MB of prebuilt native code. This browser targets phones, and WebXR
is already turned off by the build arguments.

The module is no longer added to the APK or the bundle. Code outside
the module now checks that the module is installed before it calls
into it. On an Android XR headset the browser then runs as a regular
app, without full space mode and without immersive video playback.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
